{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In <i>Island Reclamation</i>, a gripping post-apocalyptic survival game, you find yourself in a shattered world where fragmented islands hold the key to humanity's rebirth. As a resilient survivor, your mission is clear: restore power, rebuild infrastructure, and navigate the delicate balance between diplomacy and survival.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Embark on a compelling journey in &quot;Island Reclamation,&quot; a post-apocalyptic game where survival relies on rebuilding power on fragmented islands. As a resilient survivor, your task is to construct power stations to rebuild the main power lines encircling each island. However, the challenge extends to smaller settlements, where traders reside. These traders will only engage in transactions if you provide them with the power needed to operate. Fail to do so, and once-friendly settlements may turn hostile, viewing you with suspicion and mistrust.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The strategic loop intensifies as each settlement possesses a critical resource, such as the sawmill for poles. Timing becomes crucial \u2013 acquire rock, wood, iron, and more while the settlements aren't harvesting resources. Seize the opportunity when their backs are turned, deciding whether to negotiate for access or loot surrounding abandoned houses, shops, etc., to trade for gold. Use the gold to secure access to mines or acquire essential resources like wood, stone, and reliable transportation through cars .</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Building trust with communities becomes paramount \u2013 those in good standing will reward you with gold for providing power. However, for settlements harbouring mistrust, even if you provide power, the compensation in gold remains elusive. Regardless of the community's stance, they will trade with you and maintain civility as long as your firearm remains holstered. Draw your weapon, and you have only a fleeting second to stow it away before they open fire. Cars and trailers become essential for moving large items in significant quantities, overcoming a significant restriction factor in this dynamic, shattered world. Adapt your approach, navigate alliances, and decide whether to trade, loot, or embark on covert operations to meet the challenges. The fate of these islands rests squarely in your hands.</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3379750?t=1756757375","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3379750/page_bg_raw.jpg?t=1756757375","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3379750/f35427406afd23340ff99f5d7577bbe755c9fa7b/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1756757375","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3379750/f35427406afd23340ff99f5d7577bbe755c9fa7b/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1756757375","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[2,5],"notes":"Manifest369 is a post-apocalyptic survival game with frequent combat against infected creatures and occasional hostile human NPCs. Firearms and melee weapons are used; blood effects and corpses may be present. Horror elements (darkness, threat, decay) are a core theme. The game also includes non-graphic life-sim interactions (toilet and shower).\r\n\r\nSensitive topics & clarifications:\r\n\r\nDrug use: Players can grow, consume (eat), and trade cannabis as part of the in-game economy. Depiction is limited to plants/items and basic status effects; there are no addiction mechanics and no hard drugs.\r\n\r\nSexual content: None. No sexual acts, no sexual assault/non-consensual sex, no BDSM.\r\n\r\nNudity: Partial only. The player character can be undressed to underwear/boxers. No genitalia are shown. Toilet and shower interactions fade to black; no explicit nudity.\r\n\r\nViolence/Gore: Frequent combat with blood effects and ragdolls. No dismemberment or torture scenes.\r\n\r\nSelf-harm/Suicide:Suicide Only as a reset machanic.\r\n\r\nAlcohol: Not depicted and no alcohol abuse mechanics.\r\n\r\nAdditional notes:\r\n\r\nIncludes tense horror atmosphere that some players may find distressing (threat, darkness, corpses).\r\n\r\nDrug content is presented in a fictional survival context and does not endorse real-world use."},"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In <i>Island Reclamation</i>, a gripping post-apocalyptic survival game, you find yourself in a shattered world where fragmented islands hold the key to humanity's rebirth. As a resilient survivor, your mission is clear: restore power, rebuild infrastructure, and navigate the delicate balance between diplomacy and survival.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Embark on a compelling journey in &quot;Island Reclamation,&quot; a post-apocalyptic game where survival relies on rebuilding power on fragmented islands. As a resilient survivor, your task is to construct power stations to rebuild the main power lines encircling each island. However, the challenge extends to smaller settlements, where traders reside. These traders will only engage in transactions if you provide them with the power needed to operate. Fail to do so, and once-friendly settlements may turn hostile, viewing you with suspicion and mistrust.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The strategic loop intensifies as each settlement possesses a critical resource, such as the sawmill for poles. Timing becomes crucial \u2013 acquire rock, wood, iron, and more while the settlements aren't harvesting resources. Seize the opportunity when their backs are turned, deciding whether to negotiate for access or loot surrounding abandoned houses, shops, etc., to trade for gold. Use the gold to secure access to mines or acquire essential resources like wood, stone, and reliable transportation through cars .</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Building trust with communities becomes paramount \u2013 those in good standing will reward you with gold for providing power. However, for settlements harbouring mistrust, even if you provide power, the compensation in gold remains elusive. Regardless of the community's stance, they will trade with you and maintain civility as long as your firearm remains holstered. Draw your weapon, and you have only a fleeting second to stow it away before they open fire. Cars and trailers become essential for moving large items in significant quantities, overcoming a significant restriction factor in this dynamic, shattered world. Adapt your approach, navigate alliances, and decide whether to trade, loot, or embark on covert operations to meet the challenges. The fate of these islands rests squarely in your hands.</p>","developers":["ManifestStudios"],"genres":[{"description":"Action","id":"1"},{"description":"Indie","id":"23"},{"description":"RPG","id":"3"},{"description":"Simulation","id":"28"},{"description":"Strategy","id":"2"},{"description":"Early Access","id":"70"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3379750/header.jpg?t=1756757375","is_free":false,"linux_requirements":[],"mac_requirements":[],"movies":[{"highlight":true,"id":257186759,"mp4":{"480":"http://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/257186759/movie480.mp4?t=1755954472","max":"http://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/257186759/movie_max.mp4?t=1755954472"},"name":"Manifest 369","thumbnail":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/257186759/397bf2c09065924270a76f4e87e2134f38eaef2d/movie_600x337.jpg?t=1755954472","webm":{"480":"http://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/257186759/movie480_vp9.webm?t=1755954472","max":"http://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/257186759/movie_max_vp9.webm?t=1755954472"}}],"name":"Manifest369","package_groups":[],"pc_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows10/11<b